             line = line.split(iex_header_start)[1]\r\n                        return line[:4]\r\n```\r\n\r\nmypy error message: `126: error: Missing return statement`\r\n\r\nI am using mypy 0.620 and Python 3.7. I would expect mypy to recognize that barring an unforeseen/uncaught exception the method will always have a return value.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/5360/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/5360/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]